On Nov 23, 7:57 am, Philip Potter <p...@doc.ic.ac.uk> wrote:
> I like this idea. A few questions:
> 1) what happens if you are levitating?

I'm conflicted.  The boots are specifically not supposed to take
player state into account.  But they guard -steps-, and when
levitating the player isn't actually stepping.  So I lean towards the
boots being non-functional while levitating or flying.

> 2) what happens if you try to put them on while on a trap?

I'd suggest a message like "Your knees wobble uncertainly!"  Something
to indicate the player's legs trying to trip onto a different square.

> 3) would the boots let you enter Gehennom? :)

I very much like the thinking here, especially considering the
"Unspeakable cruelty and harm" prompt before entering for the first
time.  However, it would mean a player with cursed boots wouldn't be
able to continue with the game, as pit traps in the Valley of the Dead
don't penetrate (I think).

> These would be most useful in Fort Ludios, I feel :D

Ah, another unintended advantage!

